Z||000003||Archie||07-15-2001||12:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KissMySSFiero:<BR><B>can this setup be used with the stock 15 inch wheels or do you have to get bigger wheels?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>These brakes will just barely clear the 15" wheels. If the wheels have the "tape on style" wheel weights, the weights may have to be relocated.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000004||KRMFiero||07-15-2001||12:26 PM||||Archie, So What is included in the kit? What rotors and stuff do I need?   Do I have to custom make anything?<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000005||Archie||07-15-2001||06:40 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-619s.jpg">  <P>Ok, let's take a look at the parts.<BR>Large Bore Master Cylinder (92 Chevy 1/2 2WD P-Up.<BR>Rotors: Chrysler LaBaron.<BR>Front Calipers from Camaro<BR>Rear Calipers from Rear of Seville<BR>W/O H-Brake, you can use the same camaro calipers in the rear.<BR>Caliper Adapters $260 for set of 4.<BR>Brake Pads<BR>Braided Brake lines.<BR>4 each new Banjos and brake hose adapters<BR>8 New caliper bolts<P>Fabrication? Yeah you need to have your front stock Fiero rotors turned and if you decide to use the handbrake (Caddie Calipers) you'll need to make a simple bracket for the return spring.<P>BTW, before someone says that $260 is too much for the adapters, let me assure you that  YOU WANT THESE THINGS MADE CORRECTLY... Your life depends on it. Think about that when you're hacking away at making a set in your garage next weekend.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Hope this helps<P>Archie<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 07-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Patrick's Dad||07-15-2001||10:17 PM||||Hey Arch, are those available with ceramic rotors?<P>Now that I'm (finally) taking the car apart, I'm starting to think about fun stuff like this. Not knowing the Camaro, why no E-brake with Camaro calipers? Is this (The "without" version) another front caliper? If so, why doesn't the Camaro rear caliper work? If not, how different is the Camaro rear caliper?<P>RE: The Seville caliper, is it heavier? by much? Maybe it's me, but I don't see Caddy (at present) caring about things like unsprung weight.<P>Thus far, I've been looking at Wildwood calipers. They look like billet versions of my 88 calipers, but are 2.5# each. Your opinion?||||reg||3
Z||000007||onfire||07-16-2001||03:39 AM||||How much for the complete kit Archie?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/onfiresig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
